feedback_history.patient_message:
It's a weird kind of connection, isn't it? Not the deep, face-to-face intimacy I was hoping for when I first started looking online. It's more... distant but somehow profound. Like reading a letter from someone who's been through the exact same storm you are, but in a different town.

There's this quiet comfort in knowing that your pain isn't unique to you. When I read about someone else struggling with the same specific feeling of "not being where I should be," it validates everything I've been carrying. It stops me from wondering if I'm broken or if I've lost my way. Instead, it just confirms that we're all just navigating this messy, complicated terrain together.

And honestly? That validation is powerful. It reminds me that while I might feel alone in my room at night, out there, there's a whole network of people silently cheering each other on. They don't have to say it;
